//==
// # Inverse-search memos
//
// TKT-501 and TKT-404 (finding 2 of docs/plans/step-mesher-algorithmic-
// performance-2026-10-22.md): the part of a global inverse search that does
// not depend on the query point, kept once per curve, pcurve or surface and
// read by every query on it. A global search over a bounded domain samples
// the entity at parameters fixed by the domain and its breaks (SearchWindow,
// WindowCuts, PieceSamples), so the sample parameters and their points are
// the same for every query; only the distances to the query point, the
// candidates and their polish differ. On a domain with an infinite end the
// window depends on the query point (SearchWindow's doubling), so no memo is
// kept and each query samples as before.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - What is sampled
//  - Curve memos
//  - Surface memos
//  - One memo per image

//==
// # What is sampled

// The entity a curve memo samples: a space curve of the arena, evaluated as
// its record (the form ClosestParameterBySearchBody evaluates), or a pcurve,
// evaluated as its space point (the form PcurveClosestParameterBySearchBody
// evaluates).
type SearchSubject
    = SpaceCurve(Curve: CurveIndex)
    | ParameterCurve(Pcurve: PcurveIndex);

//==
// # Curve memos

// The samples of a global curve search over a bounded domain: the search
// domain (the curve's own domain for a space curve, PcurveSearchDomain for a
// pcurve), the sample parameters (PieceSamples of the window's cuts) and the
// subject's point at each. Points[i] is the subject evaluated at Samples[i],
// so Samples[0] is the domain's range start and Points[0] its point. A memo
// with no samples (NoCurveMemo) says the plain search is to be used: the
// subject has a closed-form inverse, or its domain has an infinite end.
type CurveSearchMemo
{
    Subject: SearchSubject;
    Domain: CurveDomain;
    Samples: Array<Number>;
    Points: Array<Point3D>;
}

//==
// # Surface memos

// The grid of a global surface search over a domain bounded in both
// directions: the surface's domain, the window (the domain's two ranges),
// the sample parameters along u and v (PieceSamples of each direction's
// cuts), the surface's point at each grid sample k (GridPoint(Us, Vs, k),
// row by row as ProjectBySearchBody lays them out), and the polish radius
// (one piece's width per direction). A memo with no samples
// (NoSurfaceMemo) says the plain search is to be used: the surface has a
// closed-form projection, or a direction has an infinite end.
type SurfaceSearchMemo
{
    Domain: SurfaceDomain;
    Window: SurfaceWindow;
    Us: Array<Number>;
    Vs: Array<Number>;
    Points: Array<Point3D>;
    Radius: Vector2D;
}

//==
// # One memo per image

// The memo an edge's bisection holds for one image of the edge (layer 4's
// EdgeImage): a curve memo for an image with a pcurve, a surface memo for
// one without, and Plain for an image the bisection cannot evaluate. Each
// inner memo may itself say the plain search is to be used.
type InverseMemo
    = Plain
    | OnCurve(Memo: CurveSearchMemo)
    | OnSurface(Memo: SurfaceSearchMemo);
